The current goal is to make an abstraction layer for my Minecraft "DynamX" mod, so it's indenpendant of Forge/Mc/Fabric... and on the version of the game. It'll called Hermes (Hm).
Current forge version is 1.12, and the final goal is to remove ALL net.minecraft.* and forge/fml imports from fr.dynamx.* classes. Everything should go via Hm... interfaces (like HmWorld) that are an abstract version of mc, then implemented for forge 1.12.2 in fr.hermes.forge package.
When needed, objects will be created like new ForgeSomething(mcObject) where ForgeSomething implements HmSomething and mcObject is a Something for net.minecraft. I however want to avoid doing this when possible, so we're not creating hundreds of new objets (optimisation is a matter). So keeping mapped/cached reference, for exemple for the World instances or player entities is also a goal.